Scope:

i) Has there been an assembly? Yes: F002-F005 indicate demonstrations planned in Baku on specific dates. F013 says each applicant attended one of the demonstrations. So yes, there were assemblies.

ii) Did the applicant try to participate? Yes: F013 says each applicant attended one of the demonstrations. So they did.

iii) Was the assembly peaceful? According to the applicants, the demonstrations were intended to be peaceful (F007) and were conducted in a peaceful manner (F008). There's also evidence that police dispersed them (F014) but that doesn't necessarily mean the assembly turned violent. The applicants claim peaceful. However, the state's position may argue otherwise, but we only need factual basis. The Court often looks at objective evidence; here we have the applicants' statements. There is no mention of violence. So we can conclude that the assembly was peaceful (or at least claimed to be). So scope satisfied.

Thus scope conclusion: yes.

